1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
This school bus

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,380
leaves the country

3
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:03,820
just to take kids
to high school.

4
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,000
And the school is
in the same state.

5
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:06,940
First stop:

6
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,080
Canada.

7
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,820
That’s the only road
out of

8
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,720
Point Roberts,
Washington.

9
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:14,550
That’s Blaine, right
across Boundary Bay.

10
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:16,230
It’s right there.

11
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:17,520
Unfortunately,

12
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,320
the bus is not a boat.

13
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:22,120
Why is this tip
even American?

14
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,170
In 1846,

15
00:00:24,220 --> 00:00:25,800
the Oregon Treaty
extended the border

16
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,080
along the
49th parallel.

17
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:30,850
That left the tip
on the U.S. side.

18
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:32,940
So the bus goes through
British Columbia,

19
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,600
crosses back into
the U.S. at Blaine,

20
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,900
and pulls up
to high school.

21
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,940
That’s about forty
minutes on the bus.

22
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:40,120
One way.

23
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:43,710
Then the last bell rings,

24
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,460
and they do it all again.

25
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:47,400
Into Canada.

26
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:49,140
Back into Washington.

27
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,560
Four border crossings,

28
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,770
just to go to school

29
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:53,190
in their own district.
